# CODEOWNERS — who must review a change before it can merge.
#
# Paths listed here require an explicit review from @Atroci before merging,
# enforced by this repository's branch protection ("require review from Code
# Owners"). That review is a distinct action GitHub does not let the PR's own
# author satisfy — not even from the same account, human or agent. That is
# the actual protection: an agent operating under this account can open a PR
# and push commits to it, but cannot make a PR touching these paths
# mergeable by itself.
#
# Test suites and fixtures are the software's evidence that its behavior is
# correct. A change here must not be able to quietly "fix" a failing test by
# weakening or deleting the assertion instead of the underlying bug — see
# docs/METHODOLOGY.md's review standard. Everything under every package's
# test/ directory, including fixtures, is covered.
/packages/*/test/          @Atroci

# CI workflows and this file itself. Covering .github/ means a PR that tries
# to edit CODEOWNERS (e.g. to narrow or remove this rule) is itself gated by
# the CURRENT rule's reviewer — you cannot use a PR to remove the gate that
# would otherwise apply to that same PR.
/.github/                   @Atroci
